		(uuid "2c0974d9-d451-428c-983b-f25036d0fcf8")
	)
	(text "Cord: 6 conductors (6P6C), straight or reversed.\n1 = +5V   2 = GND   3 = A   4 = B   5 = GND   6 = +5V\nSymmetric: a reversed telephone cord cannot swap +5V and GND,\nit only swaps A and B - the firmware detects it and inverts\nthe UART pads (gpio_set_inover / outover).\nJ2: the cord is soldered to the board (no jack: the board sits at 45 deg\nunder the desk edge, the cord leaves flat along the desk). Keep the\nflat order, either direction works. Cable tie through the two slots."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330.2 29.21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bde823af-9805-4bd7-8717-3016528d5016")
	)
	(text "J2: 1, 6 = +5V   2, 5 = GND (power symbols at the pins)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 345.44 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6c742ba6-c658-43c2-be33-48b8ae968326")
	)
	(text "R1 (DNP): 120R termination, only for cords over ~5 m\n(the 4.7k bias resistors on the motherboard then become 680R)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 345.44 91.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3c336884-8b18-4308-b3c5-9acc2425d492")
	)
	(text "SW1 Up  SW2 Down  SW3..SW5 presets 1..3\nTo GND, RP2040 internal pull-ups, debounced in firmware."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 322.58 125.73 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "49e0b06b-57f2-4e3b-93dc-7be9554a832a")
	)
	(text "J1: 7 = +5V (VCC)   6 = GND"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 345.44 172.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8f744234-e1b6-435e-90ec-37b276fc15c6")
	)
	(text "VCC = 5 V as before: the module regulates its own 3.3 V.\nLogic: 3.3 V from the RP2040 (SPI0, 20 MHz)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 345.44 180.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a9c2d9ce-eb36-4f57-b0af-03830931524b")
	)
	(text "Firmware: hmi_firmware/ (PlatformIO, arduino-pico).\nFirst flash: hold BOOT (SW6), plug the USB-C, release -> USB drive, copy firmware.uf2.\nLink protocol: shared/hmi_link/hmi_protocol.h (250 kbaud, motherboard polls every 10 ms).\nPCB: J1, SW1-SW5, TP2-TP6 keep their footprints; FPC_HMI1 is replaced by J2 (RJ11)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 292.1 210.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "109e39d7-6457-4c16-90ff-e7637e06e3f0")
	)
